Trained model weights and derived data
======================================

Files: web/model.json, docs/demo/model.json, and everything under experiments/,
data/processed/ and data/splits/ (the latter three are git-ignored and not published).

Training sources
----------------

The generator and the preference scorer in this repository were trained on data from

  Peter O'Donovan, Aseem Agarwala, Aaron Hertzmann.
  "Color Compatibility From Large Datasets." ACM Transactions on Graphics 30(4), SIGGRAPH 2011.
  Release: colorCode.zip, https://www.dgp.toronto.edu/~donovan/color/
  Copyright notice as it appears in the archive (README.txt):
    "Copyright (c) 2011 Peter O'Donovan
     Distributed under the Creative Commons BY-NC-SA license.
     http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.5/ca/"

  Peter O'Donovan, Aseem Agarwala, Aaron Hertzmann.
  "Collaborative Filtering of Color Aesthetics." Computational Aesthetics (CAe) 2014.
  Release: cfcolor.zip, https://www.dgp.toronto.edu/~donovan/cfcolor/
  Notice as it appears in the archive (runPrediction.m header) and on the project page:
    "Permission is granted for anyone to copy, use, modify, or distribute this program and
     accompanying programs and documents for any purpose, provided this copyright notice is
     retained and prominently displayed, along with a note saying that the original programs
     are available from our web page. The programs and documents are distributed without any
     warranty, express or implied."
  The original programs are available from https://www.dgp.toronto.edu/~donovan/cfcolor/.

The authors ask that publications using this data cite the papers above.

What license applies
--------------------

The 2011 release expressly uses CC BY-NC-SA 2.5 Canada. The license applicable to the 2014
theme and individual-rating data is unresolved: the archive carries only the permissive notice
quoted above, whose scope ("programs and documents") may or may not include the data files,
and the project page's CC BY-NC-SA sentence is inside an HTML comment attached to a withdrawn
download. Most 2014 themes (10,672 of 13,343) are also in the 2011 release and are covered by
its CC terms; the remaining themes and the individual ratings rest on the permissive notice.
This repository treats all of the 2014 data as if CC BY-NC-SA 2.5 Canada applied, as the more
restrictive reading. Written clarification has been requested from the authors.

Whether trained weights are a "Derivative Work" of a dataset under CC 2.5 Canada (section 1:
a work that "produces or reproduces the Work or any substantial part thereof in any material
form") is unsettled; float16 network weights do not reproduce any dataset row. To respect the
noncommercial condition on the training data regardless, Cory Kiser offers whatever rights he
holds in the trained weights under

  Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 2.5 Canada
  http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.5/ca/

as a licensing choice, not as confirmation of an upstream obligation. The derived parquet and
split files under data/processed/ and data/splits/ reproduce dataset rows (colors, names, IDs,
ratings) and are Derivative Works of the 2011 release; they carry CC BY-NC-SA 2.5 Canada and
are not published.

Terms in brief: use, share and adapt for noncommercial purposes, with attribution (author,
title, source URI, this notice) and a copy of or link to the license with every copy. Where
share-alike applies, adaptations must use a license permitted by section 4(b) of CC BY-NC-SA
